R spectroscopy<\/span>                                                    <\/li>\n                                    <\/ul>\n            <\/div>\n            \n            <div class=\"eael-tabs-content\">\n\t\t        \n                    <div id=\"application-description-tab\" class=\"clearfix eael-tab-content-item inactive\" data-title-link=\"application-description-tab\">\n\t\t\t\t        <p><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-5265 size-medium\" src=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/02\/aace5df3-300x234.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"234\" srcset=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/02\/aace5df3-300x234.jpg 300w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/02\/aace5df3-1024x797.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/02\/aace5df3-768x598.jpg 768w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/02\/aace5df3.jpg 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/>Fast and efficient analysis is important in the dairy industry for a number of reasons. With a well-chosen method, you can save time and material and thus significantly simplify the analysis. You can then use the measured data and saved resources to optimize the production process and improve product quality. FT-NIR spectrometers can be used to improve the control of the production process, to verify the input raw materials of intermediate products, as well as finished products, or to develop other, new technologies.<\/p>\n<p>With a single device it is possible to measure liquid, powder and pasty samples: milk, cream, buttermilk and whey, butter, cheese of all kinds, cottage cheese and cream cheese, yogurt, desserts, ice cream and milk drinks, milk powder, whey protein and more, in a matter of seconds.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_1896\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-1896\" style=\"width: 300px\" class=\"wp-caption alignleft\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-1896 size-medium\" src=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/01\/9bea2264-300x260.jpg\" alt=\"FT-NIR spectrometer Antaris II\" width=\"300\" height=\"260\" srcset=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/01\/9bea2264-300x260.jpg 300w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/01\/9bea2264.jpg 468w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-1896\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">FT-NIR spectrometer Antaris II<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>The TQ Analyst program offers you the possibility to create calibration methods, which can be used to determine a number of parameters of the measured material. These methods can be extended and modified to provide as detailed sample information as possible. The program uses advanced mathematical algorithms and allows not only the quantification of analytes in the sample, but also the classification of individual materials.<\/p>\n                    <\/div>\n\t\t        \n                    <div id=\"ft-nir-spectroscopy-tab\" class=\"clearfix eael-tab-content-item inactive\" data-title-link=\"ft-nir-spectroscopy-tab\">\n\t\t\t\t        <style>@media(max-width:1024px){.elementor-6755 .elementor-element.elementor-element-34f94d76 .dce-post-item{padding:0px 0px 20px 0px;}}@media(max-width:767px){.elementor-6755 .elementor-element.elementor-element-34f94d76 .dce-post-item{padding:0px 0px 15px 0px;}}<\/style>\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"section\" data-elementor-id=\"6755\" class=\"elementor elementor-6755 elementor-5035\" data-elementor-post-type=\"elementor_library\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-39bb9cbe elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"39bb9cbe\" data-element_type=\"section\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-no\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-5d081f3b\" data-id=\"5d081f3b\